(* The package bala2-base: the two motors and wheel encoders of the base of
   the M5Stack BALA2, an STM32 at I2C address 0x3A on the bus Wire. Grades:
   time-interval-rational, in milliseconds.

   SetMotors (left, right) sets the drives of the motors, each from -1023 to
   1023: a float, rounded to the nearest integer and clamped to that range.
   ReadEncoders () reads the counts of the encoders of the wheels, each a
   float, exact while its magnitude is at most 2^24; ResetEncoders () sets
   them to zero. The default implementations take the time of the transaction
   and read zeros.

   The base stops the motors when no SetMotors call has come for the setpoint
   window, 200 ms unless the build flag BALA2_WATCHDOG_MS sets it, and in the
   safe state of the device.

   PROVISIONAL: the bounds of the running times are estimates for the bus at
   400 kHz with the clock stretching of the STM32, to be measured on the
   device. *)

operation SetMotors : float * float ~> unit # [0.05, 2]
default SetMotors _ = delay 1/5

operation ReadEncoders : unit ~> float * float # [0.1, 2]
default ReadEncoders () = delay 1/4; (0.0, 0.0)

operation ResetEncoders : unit ~> unit # [0.05, 2]
default ResetEncoders () = delay 1/5
